note Exercism-style exercise "perfect-numbers": https://exercism.org/tracks/python/exercises/perfect-numbers
note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
note classify compares n with its aliquot sum (the sum of its divisors other than n): 1 perfect
note (equal), 2 abundant (greater), 3 deficient (smaller), 0 when n is not a positive integer.
note Check it with: sh exercise.sh exercises/perfect-numbers
om2
fn classify n long to int
if le n 0
ret 0
end
s = long 0
d = long 1
while le mul d d n bound 999999
if eq rem n d 0
if ne d n
s = add s d
end
e = div n d
if and ne e d ne e n
s = add s e
end
end
d = add d 1
end
if eq s n
ret 1
end
if gt s n
ret 2
end
ret 3
end
